{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes","id":220813,"title":"On tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-07T00:21:51-07:00","id":220813,"title":"On tribes","content":"Do the uratha need a first born totem in order to become a tribe? Will a spirit of equal power work, or does that make them merely a lodge? What's to stop more tribes from popping up? The idea of a ghost wolf tribe gets bantered around a lot in the lore, but the first born list is pretty limited (arguable if you follow the creator wolf brother of fenris sl). Perhaps a second born spirit might work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T00:45:19-07:00","id":220849,"title":"","content":"By the strictest reading... you need a First Born... but the books, as you've noted, leave plenty of options for alternatives if you want do deviate from that. Is there a reason an equally powerful spirit can't have a Tribe instead of Lodge? Not particularly from a practical sense beyond the nature of spirits in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T07:20:21-07:00","id":220992,"title":"","content":"While it's pretty clear you need a First Born, it's less clear as to how many First Born their are (before it starts, First <i>Born </i>are the Incarnae spirit children of Father Wolf, the First <i>Pack </i>are the ancestral, progenitor werewolves which are stated to be just 9 pups).<br /> <br /> So, there's really no reason you can't have another First Born be approached to be a Tribal Totem. The only thing I'd recommend is avoiding the &quot;suddenly reappeared/rediscovered Tribe&quot; thing. If you add one in, you add them retroactively or they're a brand new Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T09:06:19-07:00","id":221055,"title":"","content":"It might well be very difficult for any given werewolf to tell a Firstborn from a Secondborn (it's an actual term that's used in the books. Look it up). Werewolves might well *think* they're part of a new different tribe when a new Secondborn shows up and is subsequently convinced to give his blessing to the Uratha.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T09:23:34-07:00","id":221064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221055#post221055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might well be very difficult for any given werewolf to tell a Firstborn from a Secondborn (it's an actual term that's used in the books. Look it up). Werewolves might well *think* they're part of a new different tribe when a new Secondborn shows up and is subsequently convinced to give his blessing to the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and while it would never change the &quot;generation&quot; of this spirit, if enough Uratha start following it as a Tribal Totem, it could get even harder to tell the difference because of how much power it could accumulate with an entire Tribe behind it.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then there's all the &quot;fun&quot; that occurs when Dire Wolf and Destroyer Wolf and the others find out that one of their &quot;nephews&quot; is creating a Tribe and claiming to be a First Born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:02:40-07:00","id":221108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221064#post221064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very true, and while it would never change the &quot;generation&quot; of this spirit, if enough Uratha start following it as a Tribal Totem, it could get even harder to tell the difference because of how much power it could accumulate with an entire Tribe behind it.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then there's all the &quot;fun&quot; that occurs when Dire Wolf and Destroyer Wolf and the others find out that one of their &quot;nephews&quot; is creating a Tribe and claiming to be a First Born.</div> </div> </div> </div>*imagines a rare team-up*<br /> *shivers*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:03:01-07:00","id":221109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=220992#post220992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's pretty clear you need a First Born, it's less clear as to how many First Born their are (before it starts, First <i>Born </i>are the Incarnae spirit children of Father Wolf, the First <i>Pack </i>are the ancestral, progenitor werewolves which are stated to be just 9 pups).<br /> <br /> So, there's really no reason you can't have another First Born be approached to be a Tribal Totem. The only thing I'd recommend is avoiding the &quot;suddenly reappeared/rediscovered Tribe&quot; thing. If you add one in, you add them retroactively or they're a brand new Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we know there are at least eight, I think that is safe enough to assume lol. Now as for Second Born, how many do we know of? There are the two Wolves who are sons of Destroyer Wolf who are the Patrons of the Lodge of Garm and Lodge of Cerberus, There is that one pup of Winter Wolf, There is Blood Wolf ( who for some reason I am thinking is just another name for one of the two pups of Fenris-Ur). I know that Dire Wolf has at least one son.. but other than that, I can't think of any more. I don't think Black Wolf or Death Wolf have bore any children, same with Red Wolf, Rabid Wolf, or Silver Wolf siring any pups of their own. Now I could be completely wrong, I just don't remember lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:09:16-07:00","id":221114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221108#post221108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*imagines a rare team-up*<br /> *shivers*</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell me that's not a shiver of lip-biting anticipation D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:11:19-07:00","id":221115,"title":"","content":"Well it wasn't until you mentioned it. It was more a shiver of &quot;scary shit, that&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:14:48-07:00","id":221118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221115#post221115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it wasn't until you mentioned it. It was more a shiver of &quot;scary shit, that&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well good, it's only logical to be-<br /> <br /> Wait, did it become so just because I mentioned it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-07-2014, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:17:02-07:00","id":221119,"title":"","content":"But on tangent, I do agree it would be an interesting series of events to see one of the Second Born attempt to create a Tribe of their own. In fact, is an interesting enough of a concept that the Devs made it a possible scenario for the Ghost Wolves if they decided to create their own Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T11:06:12-07:00","id":221143,"title":"","content":"The idea of new Tribes is something that gets poked and prodded a bit in the Idigam Chronicle; one of the Hunting Grounds I wrote explores it a bit, as does one of Bunyip's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T13:17:06-07:00","id":221237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221114#post221114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please tell me that's not a shiver of lip-biting anticipation D:</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well it wasn't until you mentioned it. It was more a shiver of &quot;scary shit, that&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.reactiongifs.us/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/why_not_both.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T14:17:44-07:00","id":221262,"title":"","content":"The myth of Pangaea from the core says that there were 9 firstborn wolf spirits; only the eight tribal patrons get described. Plenty of myths regarding the ninth are scattered throughout the rest of books: Creator Wolf (who possibly became Rabid Wolf), the potential of there being two Black Wolves, Soulless Wolf (for those who want to use Bale Hounds as a tribe), Watcher Wolf (given as an example new tribal totem for Ghost Wolves) .... In addition, of course, to whatever is interesting to you. Using spirits of another choir is a pretty interesting idea, but according to Dave, spirits at that rank are &quot;spirits of an entire species&quot; : the Firstborn are slightly more elevated because Father Wolf &quot;ruled over the world&quot;, and they get plenty of power from global tribes aligned to their influences. It would make it kind of hard to find equivalent spirits willing to patron werewolves, unless the new tribe agreed to a wholly different ideology than taking up Father Wolf's mantle: which, again, I'd think is an awesome idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T14:29:35-07:00","id":221269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221118#post221118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well good, it's only logical to be-<br /> <br /> Wait, did it become so just because I mentioned it?</div> </div> </div> </div>TO be fair, it could have been anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221237#post221237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.reactiongifs.us/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/why_not_both.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who says it wasn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T14:57:23-07:00","id":221276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221262#post221262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The myth of Pangaea from the core says that there were 9 firstborn wolf spirits;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eyes back up here!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=220992#post220992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">before it starts, First <i>Born </i>are the Incarnae spirit children of Father Wolf, the First <i>Pack </i>are the ancestral, progenitor werewolves which are stated to be just 9 pups</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T15:25:46-07:00","id":221287,"title":"","content":"I always argue that soulless is the 9th and that the extra firstborn are just that. Like creator wolf and one of the black wolves, if the rumor is true. <br /> <br /> The initial firstborn are all that exist of father wolfs brood yes? There isn't a second litter somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T16:13:57-07:00","id":221313,"title":"","content":"Said it before and I'll say it again:<br /> <br /> The First Pack and the Firstborn are occasionally conflated within the text. Given that the Father Wolf myth from the corebook is explicitly the basic gist/most common variant of a bunch of different stories about the Sundering and given the periodic recounting of werewolves becoming spirits (and the existence of ancestor-spirits), I don't think this is a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T21:10:20-07:00","id":221566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221313#post221313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said it before and I'll say it again:<br /> <br /> The First Pack and the Firstborn are occasionally conflated within the text. Given that the Father Wolf myth from the corebook is explicitly the basic gist/most common variant of a bunch of different stories about the Sundering and given the periodic recounting of werewolves becoming spirits (and the existence of ancestor-spirits), I don't think this is a coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me where it states members of the First Pack being included among the First or Second Born as spirits please, I want to read those myths. I am well aware of Pure and Forsaken often being rumored to shed their physical forms and becoming true spirits upon death( thus possibly being subsumed into ancestor spirits) or when they grow powerful enough, but not in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-08-2014, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T21:26:53-07:00","id":221580,"title":"","content":"I know the maeljin can turn bale hounds into incarna. So there's one example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T21:31:24-07:00","id":221582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221580#post221580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the maeljin can turn bale hounds into incarna. So there's one example.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implied yes, though there are no examples of such transformed Uratha in Blasphemies or Lore of the Forsaken to show us that it's been done or if it's true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T21:44:10-07:00","id":221592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221566#post221566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Show me where it states members of the First Pack being included among the First or Second Born as spirits please, I want to read those myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will do absolutely no such thing because besides my conclusion being assembled holistically from putting together the various occasions where the First Pack and the pre-Sundering Firstborn-pack are described this sounds like a vaguely obnoxious demand and it gets the question exactly backwards.<br /> <br /> The First Pack aren't even <i>named</i>, and the Firstborn are many things, but their most preeminent aspect in the game is their role as <i>the spirits of the tribes.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T22:23:37-07:00","id":221617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/220813-on-tribes?p=221592#post221592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will do absolutely no such thing because besides my conclusion being assembled holistically from putting together the various occasions where the First Pack and the pre-Sundering Firstborn-pack are described this sounds like a vaguely obnoxious demand and it gets the question exactly backwards.<br /> <br /> The First Pack aren't even <i>named</i>, and the Firstborn are many things, but their most preeminent aspect in the game is their role as <i>the spirits of the tribes.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I was unaware you were the one asking my questions for me. I apologize for not writing it the way you wanted it to be presented, I shall mend my ways post haste. If my way of structuring inquiries is wrong, please instruct me on how to do it right, as you seem to be a far more literate person than I am.<br /> <br /> Now that was me being obnoxious, try to learn the difference between what is obnoxious and what is curiosity please.<br /> <br /> I was curious because I thought you might of read something I missed and I was eager to learn more. I am aware that the First Pack and First Born are conflated from time to time, but because you have an attention to details that sometimes escapes others, and I was genuinely curious and wanted to see what you knew. It turns out it was literally everything I knew already, but I'm sorry I bothered you with my questions. Now if it was a simple misunderstanding due to how I structured my sentence, I am not too proud to apologize here and now and say that I am sorry for causing this misunderstanding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/me